one could argue that the experience

254
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:45,880
has been good for him.

255
00:12:45,880 --> 00:12:48,140
Things can have a strange way of working out.

256
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:50,660
Say I wasn't the one being trained after all.

257
00:12:51,760 --> 00:12:52,880
Enough about them.

258
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:55,480
Let's get to the real reason I asked you to come here.

259
00:12:56,260 --> 00:12:59,100
I need you to travel on to the next town immediately.

260
00:12:59,560 --> 00:13:00,380
The next town?

261
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:02,660
Has something else happened on Kea Brande?

262
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:05,300
The village I chose for you as a starting point

263
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:07,820
was a relatively safe place at the time.

264
00:13:08,300 --> 00:13:08,680
However,

265
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:10,960
the Demon Lord was aware of our plans

266
00:13:10,960 --> 00:13:13,100
and sent a powerful enemy to greet you.

267
00:13:13,820 --> 00:13:14,360
And now,

268
00:13:14,360 --> 00:13:16,260
I can sense that the next village

269
00:13:16,260 --> 00:13:18,540
is in imminent danger of attack as well.

270
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:19,880
Why does it seem like

271
00:13:19,880 --> 00:13:21,400
every time she looks into the future,

272
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:22,680
it's something bad?

273
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:25,020
There will be some very important allies

274
00:13:25,020 --> 00:13:27,140
anxiously waiting on your hero's arrival

275
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,380
in the town of Seymour.

276
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:28,760
Really?

277
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:30,720
I wasn't expecting that.

278
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:31,580
It's true.

279
00:13:31,740 --> 00:13:33,940
So I ask that you hurry to meet up with them.

280
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,240
Do you think you could do that for me, Rista?

281
00:13:36,740 --> 00:13:37,680
Yes, of course!

282
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,800
I'll get right on it!

283
00:13:40,080 --> 00:13:42,080
Okay, no matter what kind of stink he raises,

284
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,540
we are going and that's final!

285
00:13:45,940 --> 00:13:46,800
Guards, your boys!

286
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:47,840
We're going to get him, Randy!

287
00:13:48,300 --> 00:13:48,580
Ah!

288
00:13:48,580 --> 00:13:56,740
Why are you going full primate on him?

289
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,660
You need to cut that crap out right now!

290
00:13:58,760 --> 00:14:00,620
I didn't ask for your opinion on my technique.

291
00:14:01,060 --> 00:14:02,840
It's part of the training anyway.

292
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:03,140
Yeah?

293
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:04,680
Well, color me surprised.

294
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,060
This is what you guys do?

295
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:08,200
You train him on your back like that?

296
00:14:09,280 --> 00:14:11,240
Why is he just laying there sobbing

297
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:12,260
and not saying anything?

298
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:13,880
You need something or what?

299
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:15,160
Yeah, in fact, I do.

300
00:14:15,420 --> 00:14:17,260
Gaea Brande is in immediate danger.

301
00:14:17,620 --> 00:14:19,160
So stop whatever you're doing here

302
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,560
because we're going right now!

303
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,220
Whatever.

304
00:14:21,520 --> 00:14:22,220
Fine with me.

305
00:14:22,580 --> 00:14:24,620
I think I've gotten all I can out of this guy anyway.

306
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:28,040
I am perfectly prepared.

307
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:29,000
That's right.

308
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,200
I'm 100% ready for this.

309
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:31,620
Great.

310
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:32,880
But first...

311
00:14:34,220 --> 00:14:37,240
Apologize to Cersei as before the trauma fully sets in!

312
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:45,900
Okay, this town is called Samal.

313
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,220
According to Ishtar,

314
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:49,100
we have allies waiting for us at the church,

315
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:50,100
so let's get over to them.

316
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:51,520
Everyone hold on what you can!

317
00:14:52,260 --> 00:14:53,860
Hold on a second, please!

318
00:14:54,220 --> 00:14:55,220
Is something happening?

319
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,720
Crane Castle to the northwest has fallen.

320
00:14:58,320 --> 00:15:00,560
This town's about to be flooded with the undead.

321
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,220
You should just keep on moving, lady.

322
00:15:04,140 --> 00:15:05,960
So, what are the undead?

323
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,920
Obviously, they're dead things that can move and attack.

324
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:10,500
Like zombies, for instance.

325
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,260
They're pretty hard to beat with just swords.

326
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,020
Well, then how do you kill them, Rista?

327
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:19,320
Fire spells and splashing them with holy water is good, too.

328
00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:20,860
Ah, holy water.

329
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:23,780
Holy water.

330
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,560
If you're dealing with those undead,

331
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:27,100
you'll need to get yourself some of that.

332
00:15:27,340 --> 00:15:29,360
So glad your shopkeepers are still around.

333
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:31,900
We can't let the undead keep us from making a living.

334
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:34,580
You'll need all you can carry,

335
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:35,980
because you don't want to run out.

336
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,000
You're right about that.

337
00:15:38,220 --> 00:15:39,380
I'll take a thousand.

338
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,420
Hey, buddy, I know you said you don't want to run out,

339
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:43,520
but this is overkill.

340
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:46,280
I mean, you just got to splash a little bit on each one of them.

341
00:15:46,440 --> 00:15:49,080
You're not going to be dunking them in this stuff or anything, you know?

342
00:15:49,420 --> 00:15:51,760
That's the reason it comes in those tiny little vials.

343
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:53,980
I don't think you could carry that many on you.

344
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:57,100
Even if you could, the weight would definitely slow you down.

345
00:15:57,280 --> 00:15:57,900
And besides,

346
00:15:58,340 --> 00:16:01,660
I don't have anywhere close to a thousand of those vials in stock today.

347
00:16:01,660 --> 00:16:03,900
Well, then you better order some right now,

348
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:06,260
because if not, I'm going to tear out that ascob, brosom.

349
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,500
Well, just take ten!

350
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:10,620
It's not enough.

351
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:11,540
It is, too.

352
00:16:11,980 --> 00:16:14,960
Besides, I'm starting to sense those undead guys getting closer.

353
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:18,120
We've got to hurry and meet our friends at the church.

354
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:19,140
Huh.

355
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:21,240
They'd better make it worth our time.

356
00:16:21,520 --> 00:16:23,360
Listen, when I talk about meeting our friends,

357
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:24,940
you're supposed to get all hyped up.

358
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:27,700
Please, don't be a jerk.

359
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:40,800
Oh, who's there?

360
00:16:41,720 --> 00:16:42,760
My stars.

361
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,200
You're a goddess, aren't you?

362
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:45,320
You must be.

363
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,840
There was a sign from God that you are coming,

364
00:16:49,120 --> 00:16:52,100
so we've been anxiously awaiting your arrival ever since then.

365
00:16:52,820 --> 00:16:54,640
These two are descendants from Dragonkin,

366
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:57,020
which means they have dragon blood in their veins.

367
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:59,020
They will be teaming up with our hero,

368
00:16:59,200 --> 00:17:01,180
and together they'll defeat the Demon Lord.

369
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:02,560
Dragonkin descendants.

370
00:17:02,880 --> 00:17:04,680
Exactly the kind of allies we want.

371
00:17:05,540 --> 00:17:06,720
Greetings, brave hero.

372
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,620
Let me introduce myself.

373
00:17:09,080 --> 00:17:11,380
I'm Father Marth, pleased to make your acquaintance.

374
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:16,520
Hey, what are you doing that for?

375
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,080
That stuff's for the bad guys!

376
00:17:18,300 --> 00:17:18,960
Oh, father!

377
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:22,660
Sayah!

378
00:17:22,660 --> 00:17:30,940
Hang on, doesn't that only happen when it's used on undead creatures?

379
00:17:31,380 --> 00:17:31,860
Crazy.

380
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:34,200
So the hero was able to tell he was one?

381
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:35,920
That's totally amazing!

382
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:41,920
I should have expected the one who killed Chaos Machina to be so cunning.

383
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:45,380
My plan was to slaughter the lot of you once I gained your trust,

384
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,880
but this changes things!

385
00:17:46,880 --> 00:17:48,900
No matter.

386
00:17:49,280 --> 00:17:52,160
I can still wipe out all of you in one fell swoop.

387
00:17:52,660 --> 00:17:55,580
My undead power was bestowed on me by Death Magla,

388
00:17:55,840 --> 00:17:58,080
one of the Demon Lord's four heavenly kings!

389
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:01,020
And now I shall use it to destroy you!

390
00:18:01,900 --> 00:18:03,140
Bring it on, you bastard!

391
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:03,780
Yeah!

392
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,680
You gotta deal with me, too!

393
00:18:05,840 --> 00:18:08,020
How long has Father Stinkmouth been at this church?

394
00:18:08,020 --> 00:18:12,640
Uh, he came over as a missionary from Crane Castle just a couple of days ago.

395
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:13,960
I see.

396
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:16,540
So this dude's not one of the local townspeople.

397
00:18:16,740 --> 00:18:17,840
What are you doing?

398
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:20,380
Get over there and help our friends make him dead again!

399
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:21,680
You don't have to yell.

400
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,300
For your information, I've already immobilized the enemy.

401
00:18:30,020 --> 00:18:30,960
What's happening?

402
00:18:30,960 --> 00:18:35,880
Look at that.

403
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:38,020
Even when I tear you apart, you don't bleed.

404
00:18:38,240 --> 00:18:39,480
You just sound constipated.

405
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:40,660
Are they all like you?

406
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:42,420
When the hell'd you cut him up?

407
00:18:42,480 --> 00:18:44,500
I didn't even see you draw your sword!

408
00:18:44,820 --> 00:18:46,600
I never saw him use his sword, either.

409
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:50,180
Maybe whatever he was doing with Circeus was actually training.

410
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:53,240
But what I really don't get...

411
00:18:53,240 --> 00:18:56,500
Hey, how could you tell he was one of those undeads, anyway?

412
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:57,820
I used my brain.

413
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:58,300
Duh.

414
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,440
So, like, how did you use it?

415
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:03,060
The priest was the oldest and most feeble person here.

416
00:19:03,500 --> 00:19:06,620
He'd be dead soonest, which means he'd also be undead soonest.

417
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:08,220
So I gave him a little shower.

418
00:19:08,820 --> 00:19:11,760
You're saying you used logic and reasoning to destroy him.

419
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,520
I don't get it!

420
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:15,280
That wasn't logical at all!

421
00:19:15,460 --> 00:19:17,700
Oh, isn't our little hero so damn clever

422
00:19:17,700 --> 00:19:20,220
while Deathmogla's undead army is gonna come put an end

423
00:19:20,220 --> 00:19:22,060
to your stupid victory celebration?

424
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:22,540
Huh?

425
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:25,740
I'm not talking about just a couple of zombies.

426
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:29,740
Tomorrow morning, there'll be 10,000 ready to eat your brains for breakfast.

427
00:19:29,740 --> 00:19:31,720
10,000 undead coming?

428
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,520
And they'll be here by the morning?

429
00:19:34,160 --> 00:19:34,640
Yeah.

430
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,920
Thanks for translating everything that we literally just heard, genius.

431
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:40,300
I'm going to need to clean this mess up.

432
00:19:41,040 --> 00:19:42,780
Since cutting you up didn't shut you up,

433
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:44,260
I'll have to be extra thorough.

434
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:46,620
Everyone run!

435
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,520
But why?

436
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:50,820
What's he doing?

437
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,180
Yes, Ron, trust me!

438
00:19:58,320 --> 00:19:59,740
Maximum Inferno!

439
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:01,640
Then there we go!

440
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:17,480
He always goes overboard on the cleanup of the finest like an afterthought.

441
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,420
Is cleanup even the right word?

442
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:30,840
He just blew it up.

443
00:20:31,280 --> 00:20:34,140
The historic church of Seymol has been reduced to rubble.

444
00:20:36,520 --> 00:20:37,780
You're welcome, sister.

445
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:40,300
I single-handedly saved all of you for free.

446
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:42,380
Yeah, because you wiped out the whole church!

447
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:44,880
And the poor nun probably just died from the shock!

448
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:46,020
That's one way to do it.

449
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,560
This guy's pretty weird.

450
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:50,500
But lucky for us, he's super strong.

451
00:20:51,200 --> 00:20:52,380
Nice to meet you, Mr. Hero.

452
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,180
My name's Mosh.

453
00:20:54,360 --> 00:20:56,040
I'm a warrior with dragonkin blood.

454
00:20:56,960 --> 00:20:58,240
And I'm Elulu.

455
00:20:58,600 --> 00:21:00,460
I've known Mosh since we were both little kids.

456
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:03,340
I'm a mage, and I also have dragonkin blood in me.

457
00:21:03,880 --> 00:21:05,700
How about we all work together, okay?

458
00:21:05,920 --> 00:21:07,560
What's your name, Mr. Hero?

459
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:08,720
Seiya.

460
00:21:09,200 --> 00:21:10,300
Seiya Ryuun.

461
00:21:10,300 --> 00:21:13,440
This one's human.

462
00:21:16,840 --> 00:21:17,880
What are you doing?

463
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:18,420
Him too.

464
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:21,180
Cool.

465
00:21:21,420 --> 00:21:21,660
Human.

466
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,900
Probably not a good idea while she's unconscious.

467
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:26,160
Hey!

468
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,960
What did you pour it on me for?

469
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:30,480
I had to be sure you hadn't turned undead at some point.

470
00:21:30,640 --> 00:21:31,200
Yeah, why?

471
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:32,840
This guy's got a trust issue.

472
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:34,520
More like a problem.

473
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:35,000
Huh?

474
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:38,020
Hey, why are you staring like that?

475
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:39,420
Yeah, what's the deal?

476
00:21:39,420 --> 00:21:41,300
You're being super creepy all of a sudden.

477
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:45,040
If these two are supposed to be our allies on this adventure,

478
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:46,520
we got to see those stats.

479
00:21:46,780 --> 00:21:48,720
This isn't what goddesses and heroes do!

480
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:50,660
You're really scaring me!

481
00:21:50,820 --> 00:21:52,320
Not all that impressive, to be honest.

482
00:21:52,740 --> 00:21:54,480
They don't have a fraction of what Seiya's packing.

483
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,260
But I guess they have room to grow.

484
00:21:56,960 --> 00:21:59,720
It'll be nice to have these guys on the team, don't you think?

485
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,460
No way.

486
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:05,300
But they have dragonkin blood,

487
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:07,920
so once they go through all the steps and learn dragon metamorphosis,

488
00:22:08,020 --> 00:22:08,620
they'll be fine!

489
00:22:08,620 --> 00:22:09,160
No way.

490
00:22:09,160 --> 00:22:39,140
Let's go.

491
00:22:39,160 --> 00:23:09,140
Let's go.

492
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:11,160
Let's go.

493
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:41,160
Let's go.

